<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wu Zetian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 690–705</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Empress Wu Zetian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wu Zetian was the only woman to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> as emperor in her own right, reigning from 690 to 705. A consort of the Tang emperors Taizong and Gaozong, she wielded power as empress and regent before proclaiming her own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>. Her reign was marked by the promotion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-examination">examination system</a>, and the Tang was restored after her abdication.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-zetian.jpg" alt="Wu Zetian" width="237" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Likely to be Zhang Xuan (张萱) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%94%90%E5%90%8E%E8%A1%8C%E5%BE%9E%E5%9C%96_(%E5%B1%80%E9%83%A8)_-_%E6%AD%A6%E5%89%87%E5%A4%A9.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
